language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session1_five_floors: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Baker, Cooper, Fletcher, Miller and Smith live on the first five floors of an apartment house, one each. Find
$ the floors where these people live, from the constraints below.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session1_five_floors.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ B: the floor of Baker (1 is the first floor, 5 the fifth)
find B : int(1..5)
$ C: the floor of Cooper
find C : int(1..5)
$ F: the floor of Fletcher
find F : int(1..5)
$ M: the floor of Miller
find M : int(1..5)
$ S: the floor of Smith
find S : int(1..5)

such that
$ they all live on different floors
allDiff([B, C, F, M, S]),
$ Baker does not live on the fifth floor
B != 5,
$ Cooper does not live on the first floor
C != 1,
$ Fletcher does not live on either the fifth or the first floor
F != 5 /\ F != 1,
$ Miller lives on a higher floor than Cooper
M > C,
$ Smith does not live on a floor adjacent to Fletcher's
|S - F| != 1,
$ Fletcher does not live on a floor adjacent to Cooper's
|F - C| != 1
